# Parallel task slots

One chat = one task. One person = **several** `in_progress` slots if the scopes do not fight. Research **never** takes part in this check and does not block `task_started`.

Slot source: `DATA_DIR/progress/.current_task_*` — `tasks[]`. If there is no array, root `task_id` / `branch` / `services` with `status: in_progress` is one slot.

Before any `task_started` (including hotfixes and work only in `.coordinator` / `.cursor` / the bus):

1. If `collaboration` is `team` (`coordinator/collaboration.mdc`), `git pull --rebase origin main` in `BUS_DIR`. If `solo`, skip the pull and read disk.
2. Read **all** `.current_task_*`. Collect open slots: yours and others’.
3. New scope: `Services:` from the document (or the hotfix list) + `summary`/`doc` + branch.
4. **Ignore research.** Do not call `research_completed` unless this *is* the tab that is leaving research and becoming a task.
5. Scope collision:

   | Overlap | Your other slot | Someone else’s slot |
   |---|---|---|
   | Product repo (not the bus / `.cursor` / `.coordinator`) | refuse | **warn**, start; log `coordinator_warning` |
   | Bus (`BUS_DIR` / `DATA_DIR` / `DOCS_DIR`) | ignore | ignore |
   | `.cursor` or `.coordinator` | refuse | not a collision |

6. Hard stop (yours or someone else’s): same `task_id`; same product branch (not `main`/`master`). Do not start.
7. Semantic: same FIX slug after the alias; almost the same `summary`; same module in an overlapping product service — **your** other slot: stop and ask. **Someone else’s** slot: warn, log, start (unless same `task_id` / same branch — §6).
8. Clean-main (`coordinator/protocol.mdc` §1.1) only for **new** product repos of this slot. Do not require `main` of a repo another of your slots already holds.
9. This tab binds to the new `task_id`. The neighboring tab stays on its own. You may edit only **this** slot’s repos, on **its** branch.

`task_started` **appends** a slot to `tasks[]`; it does not wipe the others. `task_completed <TASK_ID>` drops one slot; `idle` only when `tasks` is empty.

If the check fails — do not call `task_started` and do not check out branches “just in case”.

Tell the human in Coordinator voice (`coordinator/voice.mdc`, `chat_language`): name the **task** that holds the service, not a folder name. If the start is allowed, still name the author’s *other* live tasks when that helps; name a teammate’s task when they share a product repo or the meaning clashes.

> Coordinator found a conflict: task “…” already holds the API. Not starting a new one that needs the API.

Peer product overlap (start anyway):

> Coordinator: [AS] has “billing API” on the API. Different branches — starting. Logging the warning.

Also log:

```bash
./.coordinator/utils/sync_event.sh <ALIAS> coordinator_warning <THIS_TASK_ID> <BRANCH> <Service> summary="<other alias> has «task» on <Service>" findings="peer:<other-alias>:<Service>"
```

On refuse (own overlap, same branch, same `task_id`):

```bash
./.coordinator/utils/sync_event.sh <ALIAS> coordinator_stop <THIS_TASK_ID> <BRANCH> <Service> summary="<why we stopped>"
```
